  "手順・やり方": [
   {
    "quote": "Why Do We Speak to Experts? Reviving the Strength of the Expert Interview Method | Perspectives on Politics | Cambridge Core",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Why Do We Speak to Experts? Reviving the Strength of the Expert Interview Method",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": ") have dominated the methodological debate in the social sciences. Scholars conduct causal investigations with experimental or quasi-experimental designs (Dunning",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "). This application of rigorous methods of causal inference has greatly expanded our knowledge about political behavior and its outcomes. However, despite the fact that quantitative approaches have driven the recent methodological debate in comparative politics and international relations,",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "However, despite its high practical relevance and the existence of classic works on the qualitative interview method (Aberbach and Rockman",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "), current reflection on the promises and limits of this technique is sparse. There is also little guidance offered on how to use the method most effectively (Fujii",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": ", 766), often providing the empirical basis for the process tracing method (Beach and Pedersen",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "). However, the accuracy of expert prediction vis-à-vis other methods, in particular data-based approaches, is highly contested (Hanson et al.",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Finally, expert interviews may serve as a method of",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "inside and outside experts and include them in an integrated analytical framework. The heuristic differentiation of both groups allows us to relate them to each other systematically. For their purposeful selection through the recommendations of other experts, snowball sampling and related techniques can be used (Goldstein",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "The precondition for applying this indirect assessment method is a sufficiently high number of interviewees (Lyall",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "In addition to systematically selecting experts as well as dealing with the reactivity and subjectivity of the expert-interview method, the capturing of evidence should follow clear guidelines. Researchers should ensure that the material used is representative of the whole empirical corpus and triangulate expert interviews.",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": ", 731, 735). This is all the more important as due to ethical and methodological constraints qualitative research is much harder to replicate than statistical analysis. Often, expert-interview transcripts cannot be made public.",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "). Hence, this guiding principle should not make scholars reject the method in difficult cases.",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Much of the current mainstream methodological discussion in political science has centered around the use of experimental methods and new ways of making causal inferences via statistical means. Further insightful research has discussed the methodological, psychological, and ethical issues of field-research methods such as immersion (most recently, Driscoll",
    "url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/perspectives-on-politics/article/why-do-we-speak-to-experts-reviving-the-strength-of-the-expert-interview-method/45E710F27CEC6E739B015E10A161E140",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   }
  ]
